            <widget class="QLabel" name="tool_label">
             <property name="text">
              <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Steps:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Load set of 3D NIFTI images acquired at different frequency offsets. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Load CEST offsets. The number of CEST offsets defined must equal number of loaded images. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Load mask. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Type valid filename and save 4D image. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;This widget concatenates the 3D images and save sa 4D volume with the 4th dimension being the frequency axis. During this process, it will normalize the signal by the -300 ppm image. The -300 ppm image is assumed to be the &lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;first image in the loaded series.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
             </property>
